      "name": "I2rlearning",
      "created_at": "2025-08-28T10:52:23.087Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I have a user who only has access to their timesheet(s) and no one else’s (this part works great).  However, within the timesheet the user needs access to a particular field that we are pulling into the timesheet from the project doctype.</p>\n<p>In the role manager permissions manager I have add the project doctype with nothing selected, but it gives me an error.  When I select read only it works in the timesheet but then they can see the project doctype.  I have even tried this project type also to no avail.</p>\n<p>What I am wanting to achieve is to hide project from their view and yet still give a user access to read from it. Is this possible?  I do not want to go field by field adding a permission level of 2 for example. That seems like too much work. I am open to any ideas.</p>",
